Title: Designed Once, Usable Everywhere: An Investment in PHP’s Standard Library
Publication date: Nov 03, 2026

Short summary:
The post argues for small, carefully designed additions to PHP's standard library to reduce duplicated, incompatible userland solutions. It highlights PHP 8.6 additions such as a SortDirection enum and a Time\Duration class, explains how these types unify APIs (with examples for sorting and timeouts), and describes planned follow-ups (e.g., Time\Instant / Time\Clock). The author also discusses the importance of careful RFC design, long-term maintenance, and invites the community to test, adopt, contribute to, or fund this work.

